    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but isn't it a bit reductive to say one is just \"more sound\" than the other? A lot of people argue that retributive justice is actually the only way to truly honor the victim and ensure accountability—that without actual punishment, there's no justice at all. Isn't that view just as morally valid?",
